    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.33.3</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:37:11 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>23303</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.33.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><p><strong>Quitting is quitting.</strong></p><ul><li>When macOS or a script asks Squeak to quit (a kill signal), it now quits normally instead of being cut off, so it no longer reports a false "closed unexpectedly" next time.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.33.2</h4><p><strong>The room is the room; your chats stay yours.</strong></p><ul><li>A pond's Room shows only what was said in the room and the ducks' own posts. Direct chats with a duck stay out.</li><li>The Room header shows only ducks on duty.</li><li>In ducks mode the new-chat page never offers Main; the "+" in a duck's chat starts a chat on that duck's branch.</li><li>Ducks can branch off again (they were told "Placement is unavailable here").</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.33.1</h4><p><strong>Chats always work on their own branch.</strong></p><ul><li>A new chat in a git pond starts on its own branch, so Skip approvals no longer asks for every command. A chat still in Main moves to its own branch when you write to it, and the app opens the new chat.</li><li>A duckling sent back to work shows as working again until it reports.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
